From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LosDaemons13 <esteveloris@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:13:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader split: large pool batches come back through a file on
 Windows

A pool result goes back to the parent in one pipe write, and on Windows
that write fails above 4 GiB (OSError: [WinError 87], CPython's
_winapi.WriteFile; a 3.94 GiB result passes, a 4.06 GiB one fails, Python
3.12). A batch of 16 of Pokemon Pokopia's files carried more shader code
than that, so its split ended at 79/79 with nothing written.

scan_batch now pickles a batch whose shader bytes pass SPILL_BYTES (1 GiB)
to a file beside the shader map (DM_SPLIT_SPILL_DIR), and pooled reads it
back and removes it as soon as that batch is done. Smaller batches go
through the pipe as before. The deferred Unity pass goes through the same
path. Checked on Pokopia 2.0.1's files on Windows: the split that failed
now gets past every file.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Windows builds of games with more than 4 GiB of shader code in one batch (Pokemon Pokopia) failed in the shader split
Issue: none yet (LosDaemons13/NX2Apple, a Windows build of Pokemon Pokopia)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
